  {
   "key": "0x18..0x19",
   "name": "envelope generator",
   "aliases": [
    "envelope control",
    "En"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
     "lines": "404-405"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
     "lines": "455-486"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
     "lines": "178-202"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/saa1099.cpp",
     "function": "saa1099_device::data_w",
     "case": [
      "0x18"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/mame/saa1099.cpp",
     "lines": "439-448"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Registers 18 and 19 are envelope generators 0 and 1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "404-405",
       "sha": "a35d4449cd5809642bbbbb859e1b28eb3cefc021f19be0107548f3d24e3f8ce5"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "455-457",
       "sha": "3a0f8a4824d2913923464a1063cfd2b3848a0b02a8523b6b051672a543c8dcf0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The table gives one bit whose 0 leaves both components the same envelope and whose 1 inverts the right; its label is garbled in the capture.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "456-460",
       "sha": "e1b1f831393535a13396d485ba1c494f0558a4e01824ca15a79d203c40a9f0bb"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "193-194",
       "sha": "509b54469b7ddc913e6d39f8bebe4b0d9b3efa202508d6ea0a86abf73ec65d9d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Three mode bits select one of eight modes: zero, maximum, single or repetitive decay, single or repetitive triangular, single or repetitive attack; the bit labels are garbled.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "461-471",
       "sha": "2025ab6da66ff543c684c744b3352c13a84f096d9abda9a0444132792df52817"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The table gives four bits of envelope control at up to 977 Hz and three bits at up to 1,95 kHz; the bit labels are garbled in the capture.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "476-477",
       "sha": "6ae9a35dafa9e6c418f86214d8aebe3ebc5ce1fb706d171ce83592294de30766"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The table gives an internal envelope clock from frequency generator 1 or 4 and an external one from the address write pulse; the bit labels are garbled.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "480-481",
       "sha": "0f5c8dbbd25cfafca78669b1012a69fbd84dcffed969d5d8cc55ec6de79ba043"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The timing is programmable from a frequency generator, and the mode halves the resolution to eight levels by rounding down.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "190-192",
       "sha": "7a6b646431b365827ccb657a1d29f454c26875cb82c80fc6d85806af43869b98"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Two of the six tone generators are under envelope control, on both their outputs.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "178-180",
       "sha": "1bfebe045717b613b7c2f96041f8c8278d7a6328fa574f45818dd37a6055c48e"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The eight envelope modes run from zero amplitude to continuous attack-decay.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "181-189",
       "sha": "452a4cf84c61df5130d2f9748cfad21ee3e6b29297d14a5de21232378f2c376a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "10",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A direct enable starts an envelope and can terminate it at any time.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "195-196",
       "sha": "80659e96d850f407e36328c331237907544785b10bae9e64d6d3e55b7aad384a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "11",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With the frequency channel off the envelope itself appears at the output as a non-square tone.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "197-199",
       "sha": "e5a796eeb547fbd607a8f2881d2233400c4bfaa03ef53ec55a414b6c30d2bd19"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "12",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Rates quoted are for an 8 MHz clock; halved resolution reaches up to 2 kHz.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "200-202",
       "sha": "5ad06d86a85c305a5273f4bb7d1796442511574c09aade34a03344e118de9f75"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A write to register 18 or 19 holds the envelope control bits: E07 to E00 in register 18, E17 to E10 in register 19, bit 6 unused.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:SAA1099.raw.txt",
       "lines": "404-405",
       "sha": "a35d4449cd5809642bbbbb859e1b28eb3cefc021f19be0107548f3d24e3f8ce5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
